e of community energy  remains putting solar on rooftops this  is happening all over the country with a  variety of different models sometimes  it's independent community energy  organizations doing it themselves  sometimes they're they use umbrella or  support organizations like solar for  schools share energy or energy for all  this is a great first step and something  i certainly encourage many of you who  don't know how to get started with  energy in your communities to look at  there are also numerous organizations  around the country providing fuel  poverty and energy advice services which  is a key one and is often for those of  you who here from local authorities  can really help to meet the the  objectives and  requirements of local authorities um the  services like this are often provided  often funded by the surplus income from  generating renewable electricity  there is much more to the sector though  and as well as new and innovative  business models which are emerging  so i'll start with energy efficiency  i've got a few examples so people  powered retrofit is a not-for-profit  service for householders in greater  manchester  offering clear independent advice to  support and help people plan procure and  deliver home retrofits retrofit is when  you make changes to a house or a  building to increase its energy  efficiency  um people-powered retrofit is trying to  tackle the key barriers that a lot of  homeowners face in commissioning work  such as lack of appropriate contractors  concerns about the quality of the work  that we carried out and a lack of local  markets for this kind of energy  efficiency work  so they're halfway to raising 550 000  pounds in a community share offer  um just showing that the kind of the the  demand for that kind of service but also  um hopefully you can see that the the  kind of work that they do is is not  geographically specific it's something  that is important everywhere this  country needs retrofit everywhere  another