gy where is the sector going our  energy energy system is changing  increased local generation and storage  electrification of heating and transport  systems and the rise of flexibility  services to help balance the grid in  real time are all happening now and  they'll shape the future of energy  infrastructure and the way it meets our  needs and how we interact with it  if we're to develop a truly innovative  and effective future energy system  people whether that's community groups  houses or businesses must be put at the  heart of the energy system  last year we published our 2030 vision  which was based on a detailed  consultation process with community  energy practitioners and project  projections from a report by wpi  economics about what the sector can  achieve the vision sets out our  understanding of the dimensions of a  cohesive zero carbon energy system with  empowered communities at the center and  you can access that it's free on our  website graphics like this and the  previous slides are all part of it um so  i encourage you to use that to help  in your communities  as well as driving the transition to  renewable energy increasing energy  efficiency and reducing fuel poverty at  the ground level  community energy organizations around  the country are active partners in  sophisticated innovation projects and  trials  i'm going to give a couple of examples  hopefully to inspire you about what you  might be able to get involved with  so in the midlands chase community  sailor is part of the zero carbon  rougely consortium which is developing  smart local energy system encompassing 7  000 homes 400 commercial premises and  two railway stations using numerous  integrated energy solutions that will be  designed and digitally operated at local  level  as you can see much bigger scale to the  usual work of community energy  historically  another one is project leo in  oxfordshire not as far away  which is a holistic smart grid trial in  which community energ